FakeRAM2.0: a filegroup so bazel can stage the vendored tool.

AUTO_MEMORIES generates its .lib/.lef views by calling FakeRAM:

    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, fakeram_run,
                           "--orfs_asap7_backend", ...])   # gen_memories.py

ORFS vendors FakeRAM at tools/FakeRAM2.0 and, since ORFS #4603, ships
it with the ASAP7 backend already applied. What it does not ship is a
label: the tool has to be staged into the canonicalize sandbox, and
that needs a package. This adds a single
filegroup(name = "all_files", srcs = glob(["**/*"])) -- the BUILD.bazel
hunk of ORFS's old patches/fakeram backend patch, the one part of it
#4603 did not fold in -- so bazel-orfs does not have to generate a BUILD
file of its own, and orfs_source.bzl's "these two packages are the
whole non-design coupling surface" stays true. orfs_source.bzl's
_UNIGNORE_FAKERAM makes the package loadable despite ORFS's
.bazelignore.

Not upstreamed: ORFS does not build with bazel any more, so the file
has no consumer there. Retires if ORFS grows a BUILD file for
tools/FakeRAM2.0, or if bazel-orfs stages the tool another way.

diff --git a/tools/FakeRAM2.0/BUILD.bazel b/tools/FakeRAM2.0/BUILD.bazel
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/FakeRAM2.0/BUILD.bazel
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+filegroup(
+    name = "all_files",
+    srcs = glob(["**/*"]),
+    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
+)
